WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.210
From a live-action Disney adaptation to some
of the biggest sci-fi films of the year, March

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:08.900
is stacked with movies well worth checking
out at the box office.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:13.540
Update your calendar, fill your pockets with
snacks, shovel your car out of the snow, and

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.780
check out this onslaught of March movies.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.280
Logan

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:23.440
Director James Mangold's Logan really could
be Hugh Jackman's last hurrah as Wolverine.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:28.660
The film is a loose adaptation of Marvel's
Old Man Logan comics arc, and will dive into

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.760
the darker side of the X-Men universe's possible
future.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:37.120
The film also features fan-favorite Wolverine
clone X-23's big-screen debut.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:41.940
The story finds an aged Wolverine, with a
failing healing factor and broken spirit,

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.840
protecting an older Professor X at the end
of his life.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.160
The early trailers look fantastic, and Jackman
even took a pay cut to ensure the filmmakers

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.460
would have the flexibility to create the R-rated
story properly.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.960
Get ready for the end on March 3rd.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:57.800
Before I Fall

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:03.320
Think of it like Groundhog Day, but a lot
bleaker, and for the teen girl set.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:09.300
This sci-fi-lite drama is based on the 2010
novel of the same name by Lauren Oliver, and

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:14.120
follows a 17-year-old girl who has to relive
the day of her death over and over until she

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:15.820
figures out how to get it "right."

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:21.260
Young Sam, played by Zoey Deutch, uses her
time loop to try and avoid her fate, and eventually

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:25.740
finds the freedom to take chances — and
learns there's a lot more to life than she thought.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.360
Check it out on March 3rd.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:28.960
And then check it out again.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.040
And again.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:30.960
And again.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:33.480
T2: Trainspotting 2

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:38.680
It's been more than 20 years, but director
Danny Boyle is back with the long-awaited

00:01:38.689 --> 00:01:44.000
sequel to his cult-hit-black-comedy-crime-drama,
complete with original stars Ewan McGregor,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.180
Ewen Bremner, Jonny Lee Miller, and Robert
Carlyle.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:52.120
Expectations are high for Boyle to follow
up his modern classic, but by loosely basing

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:56.620
the story on the original novel's sequel,
Porno, he at least has a template to follow.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:01.500
Reviews have been largely positive in the
UK, where T2 is already in theaters.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.940
Spot it in the US on March 3rd.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.240
Kong: Skull Island

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:12.560
Hollywood's most famous angry ape, aside from
Gary Busey, returns to the big screen on March

00:02:12.569 --> 00:02:18.780
10th, alongside A-listers Tom Hiddleston,
Samuel L. Jackson, John Goodman, John C. Reilly,

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:19.680
and Brie Larson.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:24.680
The plot seems fairly predictable, but still
relentlessly fun: a team of explorers and

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:29.510
soldiers venture onto an uncharted island
in the Pacific, which just happens to include

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:30.860
a whole lot of monsters.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:32.840
"I call them skullcrawlers."

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:33.480
"Why?"

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:36.280
"I never said that name out loud before.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.100
Sounds stupid now that I say it, just --- you
call them whatever you want."

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:43.980
Legendary is reportedly looking to combine
the worlds of Kong and Godzilla for the first

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:49.069
time since their first showdown in 1962, so
this one should also help set the stage for

00:02:49.069 --> 00:02:50.840
even more monster insanity.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.220
You just know they're gonna bring the big
guy back to New York, right?

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:56.000
The Belko Experiment

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:01.019
This high-concept horror film was written
by Guardians of the Galaxy's James Gunn and

00:03:01.019 --> 00:03:05.709
follows a group of 80 white-collar office
workers trapped in a violent social experiment

00:03:05.709 --> 00:03:09.090
in which the work day suddenly becomes a life-or-death
game.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:14.489
It's basically Glengarry Glen Ross meets Battle
Royale meets Saw, and features a long list

00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:18.410
of familiar faces getting spattered with the
blood of their co-workers.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:23.420
So if you ever wanted to actually see John
McGinley from Office Space going HAM in an office...

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.660
get your TPS reports in by March
17th.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:28.340
Beauty and the Beast

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:33.180
If you're a living, breathing human being,
you already know the story of Beauty and the

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:36.769
Beast, so you're probably not in for any huge
surprises.

00:03:36.769 --> 00:03:41.269
Disney has realized that turning its animated
classics into live-action blockbusters is

00:03:41.269 --> 00:03:46.440
pretty big business, and this marks the latest
installment of more than 20 planned adaptations.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:51.720
Like usual, the Mouse House has assembled
an all-star cast, including Emma Watson, Dan

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:56.800
Stevens, Luke Evans, and a whole lot of computers
to make that talking clock believable.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.820
Your furry fantasies come to life on March
17th.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.360
Free Fire

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:07.840
This action comedy from High-Rise director
Ben Wheatley stars Brie Larson, Sharlto Copley,

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:12.550
Armie Hammer, Cillian Murphy and Jack Reynor
as a bunch of criminals who get stuck in an

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.540
arms deal gone terribly wrong.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:19.600
A disagreement turns into a shootout, violent
comedy ensues, and if early buzz is to be

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.640
believed, it's full of punchy laughs and a
high injury count.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:26.380
Free Fire is set to launch in the US on March
17th.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.900
King Arthur: Legend of the Sword

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:34.400
Guy Ritchie is taking a break from his Sherlock
Holmes franchise to put a fresh spin on the

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.140
classic story of King Arthur.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:41.300
Due out March 24th, the story follows a young
Arthur who learns about his royal lineage

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.740
after pulling Excalibur from its stone.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:48.220
With great sword comes great responsibility,
and Arthur has to make some tough decisions.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:54.100
"I'm happy to talk, but there's no way that
I am fighting."

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:59.100
Despite its obvious period setting, the film
looks like a more modern, action-filled take

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.820
on the classic story, filled with A-list talent.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:03.640
Power Rangers

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:09.000
For adults of a certain age, the re-imagining
of the Power Rangers franchise has been a

00:05:09.009 --> 00:05:10.090
long time coming.

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:15.660
The '90s kids' series is getting a big-screen
reboot as a PG-13 action franchise, so if

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:20.080
you've ever wanted to see Bryan Cranston as
a giant disembodied head, your dreams come

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.420
true on March 24th.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:26.800
Director Dean Israelite has put together a
nice mix of stars, including Elizabeth Banks,

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.660
and a team of young up-and-comers to play
the teenage Rangers.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:34.460
Israelite's previous film, Project Almanac,
did a good job with its teen protagonists,

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:37.599
so this one has the potential to be a whole
lot of fun.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:41.600
One thing's for sure: if Bulk and Skull don't
make a cameo, we riot.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:43.060
Life

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:48.800
This sci-fi horror thriller follows a team
of astronauts who retrieve a Mars space probe

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:49.940
with a sample inside.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:54.539
Because nothing good ever comes from Mars,
all hell breaks loose and the crew has to

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:59.080
find a way to stop the space monster while
trapped on board the International Space Station.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:05.360
If it sounds like Alien, well...that's because
it pretty much is, Alien — with a twist.

00:06:05.369 --> 00:06:10.499
The cast of doomed spacemen includes Jake
Gyllenhaal, Rebecca Ferguson, Ryan Reynolds,

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:11.540
and Hiroyuki Sanada.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.540
Get probed on March 24th.

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:14.880
CHiPS

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:21.120
This buddy cop comedy stars writer/director
Dax Shepard and Michael Peña as two California

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:26.260
Highway Patrol motorcycle officers who investigate
a corrupt police department by making at least

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.429
one weiner joke every three minutes.

00:06:28.429 --> 00:06:33.900
Sure, CHiPS is a comedy-centric remake of
the 1970s TV drama, but that worked out pretty

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:35.480
well for 21 Jump Street.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:38.340
"My name's Jeff."

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:40.660
"That's Jefe, man."

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:44.800
Remember how much you liked the Starsky and
Hutch and Dukes of Hazzard movies?

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:48.940
Well, even if you didn't, there's still a
lot of talent and potential here.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:50.680
Ride or die on March 24th.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:52.400
Ghost in the Shell

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:57.559
The long-awaited live-action adaptation of
this acclaimed manga and anime looks like

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:00.120
one of the most ambitious sci-fi films of
the year.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:05.740
Scarlett Johansson, no stranger to skin-tight
action, stars as the cyborg Major, as she

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:09.740
and her counter-cyberterrorist unit they take
on cyber-saboteurs.

00:07:09.749 --> 00:07:13.919
The film looks to be a gorgeous translation
of the visuals from the anime, so no matter

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:18.940
how it turns out, there seems to be no doubt
director Rupert Sanders has built something gorgeous.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:22.500
Ghost in the Shell gets uploaded to theaters
on March 31st.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:24.000
Thanks for watching!

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:27.140
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:29.840
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

